  "summary": "Five candidate documents directly apply federated learning (decentralised training without pooled records) or closely related methods to hate speech detection. The strongest matches are those combining the federated/decentralised method with the hate speech topic. [V0107] (Adebayo et al., 2026) applies decentralised training without pooled records to hate speech detection on the ProtMap dataset, achieving 0.94 AUROC. [V0105] (Gupta et al., 2024) applies the same federated approach to hate speech detection on ToxiBench, reporting 0.80 accuracy. [V0108] (Brennan et al., 2018) is a deployment study of decentralised training without pooled records for hate speech detection on FireScope, achieving F1=0.66. [V0106] (Haddad et al., 2025) applies decentralised training without pooled records to hate speech detection on GridWatch, reporting a test MAE of 0.87. As a fifth entry, [V0110] (Adebayo et al., 2026) applies boosted decision-tree ensembles (not federated learning) to hate speech detection on GridWatch, achieving 0.63 AUROC; it is included as the next-best hate-speech-detection candidate, though its method does not match the federated learning criterion as precisely as the others.",
